  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 243 AM MDT Mon Sep 28 2026\n\nUpper-level trough will continue shifting eastward today, with \nshowers and isolated thunder across eastern Idaho through this \nevening. Expect a 10 degree cooldown for many locations between \nyesterday's daytime temperatures and today's, with highs only \nwarming into the 50s and 60s for much of the forecast area. Models \nsuggest high pressure building in from the west beginning Tuesday, \nremaining in control of the pattern through the end of the extended \ntimeframe. This will mean dry conditions for the next week and \ngradual warming. Daytime temperatures will warm into the low to mid-\n70s across low elevations by Thursday with some locations likely \nreaching 80 degrees by early next week.",
